  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know that,&nbsp;the Molar mass of Carbon=12</p><p>Molar mass of Hydrogen=1</p><p>Molar mass of Oxygen=16</p><p>Empirical formula mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p><p>Molecular mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>&#160;Molccular Mass&#160;</mtext><mtext>&#160;Empirical formula mass&#160;</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>30</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math>&nbsp;Molecular formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#215;</mo></math> empirical formula</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Molecular formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math></p>"
